    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Download.FixAuthlib.ToolTip">Some versions, including 1.16.5, may disable multiplayer when an offline account is used. PCL can update Authlib to correct this.&#x0a;This affects only newly installed instances.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Download.InstallBehavior">Install behavior</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Download.SpeedLimit">Speed limit</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Download.SpeedLimit.ToolTip">Limits download speed so other apps can continue using the network smoothly.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Download.TargetFolder">Target folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Download.TargetFolder.Hint">Change the destination in Launch → Choose Instance → Folder List.&#x0a;Right-click a folder or instance to open it in File Explorer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Download.Threads">Maximum threads</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Download.Threads.ToolTip">More threads can improve speed when a server limits each connection, but very high values may make the launcher less responsive.&#x0a;64 threads is enough for most downloads.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Source.File">File download source</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Source.PreferOfficialThenMirror">Prefer official sources; use mirrors when slow</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Source.Title">Game Resources</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Source.UseMirror">Prefer mirrors</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Source.UseOfficial">Prefer official sources</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Source.Version">Version list source</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.GameManage.Source.Version.Mirror">Prefer mirrors (new releases may appear later)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.AutoRepairGame">Repair missing mod dependencies automatically</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.AutoRepairGame.ToolTip">After a crash, PCL can detect missing mod dependencies, install them, and try launching again. Turn this off to show crash analysis only.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.DisableJlw">Disable Java Launch Wrapper</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.DisableJlw.ToolTip">Java Launch Wrapper helps older Java versions start from paths containing Chinese characters.&#x0a;Turn it off only when anti-cheat software blocks it or it causes another problem.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.DisableLwjglUnsafeAgent">Disable LWJGL Unsafe Agent</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.DisableLwjglUnsafeAgent.ToolTip">Minecraft 26.1 uses LWJGL 3.4.1, whose FFM-based native memory access can perform poorly on JDK 25 or later. PCL enables LWJGL Unsafe Agent to avoid this issue.&#x0a;Disable it temporarily only when troubleshooting. This option applies only to LWJGL 3.4.1.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.DisableRw">Disable RetroWrapper</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.DisableRw.ToolTip">RetroWrapper improves compatibility and usability for Minecraft 1.5.x and earlier.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.GameTail">Additional game arguments</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.GameTail.ToolTip">Appends these values to the game arguments. For example, --demo starts Minecraft in demo mode.&#x0a;Minecraft JSON tokens such as ${library_directory} are supported.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.GpuPreference">Use the high-performance GPU</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.GpuPreference.ToolTip">Sets Java to High performance in Windows Settings → System → Display → Graphics.&#x0a;On systems with integrated and dedicated graphics, this helps Minecraft use the dedicated GPU.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.JvmHead">Additional JVM arguments</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.JvmHead.Restore">Restore Defaults</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.JvmHead.ToolTip">Adds JVM arguments when Minecraft starts. Change these only when you understand their effect.&#x0a;Minecraft JSON tokens such as ${library_directory} are supported.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.MoreInInstanceSetup">More options are available in each instance’s settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.PreLaunchCommand">Run Before Launch</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.PreLaunchCommand.ToolTip">Runs a command or program before Minecraft starts. Use Windows Command Prompt syntax.&#x0a;&#x0a;Path tokens (each path ends with \):&#x0a;· {path}: PCL executable folder&#x0a;· {minecraft}: .minecraft folder&#x0a;· {verpath}: Instance folder (.minecraft\versions\instance-name\)&#x0a;· {verindie}: Instance folder when isolation is on; .minecraft folder otherwise&#x0a;· {java}: Java runtime folder&#x0a;&#x0a;Other tokens:&#x0a;· {user}: Player name&#x0a;· {login}: Login method&#x0a;· {uuid}: Player UUID&#x0a;· {name}: Instance name&#x0a;· {date}, {time}: Current system time&#x0a;· {version}: Vanilla version&#x0a;&#x0a;Examples:&#x0a;· &quot;{verpath}test.exe&quot;&#x0a;· &quot;{java}java.exe&quot; -jar &quot;{verpath}test.jar&quot;&#x0a;· notepad &quot;{verindie}options.txt&quot;&#x0a;&#x0a;Put paths in double quotation marks when they may contain spaces. The working directory is the current .minecraft folder.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.PreLaunchCommand.Wait">Wait for the command to finish</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup.Launch.Advanced.Renderer.DirectX12">DirectX 12 (D3D12)</sys:String>
